</div><a id="KBYG"></a><a id="CP_JUMP_7481426"></a><div id="cs_control_7481426" class="cs_control CS_Element_Custom"><style>blockquote {border-left: 5px solid #fff;}</style>
<div class="Component ArticleTextGroup TextWrapped clearfix">
<h2>Know Before You Go</h2>
</div></div><div id="cs_control_7475379" class="cs_control CS_Element_Custom"><style>blockquote {border-left: 5px solid #fff;}</style>
<div class="Component ArticleTextGroup TextWrapped clearfix">
<figure class="-auto-width">
<picture>
<source type="image/webp" srcset="/subjects/healthandsafety/images/KBYG_banner_text.png?maxwidth=1300&autorotate=false&quality=78&format=webp">
<img alt="A graphic of a visitor at home sitting at a desk using a laptop computer. On the left, a sign reads &quot;Start Here.&quot; To the visitor&#39;s right, an open backpack is next to the visitor." src="/subjects/healthandsafety/images/KBYG_banner_text.png?maxwidth=1300&autorotate=false" title="KBYG Banner"  >
</picture>
</figure><!-- floating-image alignment  -->
<h4>“If you don’t know where you are going, you’ll end up someplace else.” <em>-Yogi Berra</em></h4>
<p>Researching ahead of time gives you the opportunity to learn about the park and the environment(s) you’ll encounter during your adventure. You’ll have time to prepare and get the right gear/equipment needed for you and anyone that may be traveling with you. Keep reading to learn about what you should "Know Before You Go":</p>
</div></div><div id="cs_control_7475302" class="cs_control CS_Element_BulletedList"><div class="Component accordion-list-component">
<div id="accordion7475302" class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered">
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475318_2">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475318_2">
Learn about the park
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475318_2"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475318_2">
<p>Every park environment is unique and continuously changing with the seasons. <a href="https://www.nps.gov/findapark/index.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/findapark/index.htm|">Visit the park's website</a> on <a href="https://www.nps.gov/index.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/index.htm|">NPS.gov</a> or the <a href="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/digital/nps-apps.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/digital/nps-apps.htm|">NPS mobile app</a> to become familiar with the places you will visit. Consider the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Amenities</strong> - Does the park have drinking water, park shuttles, or stores where you can buy food and gear?</li>
<li><strong>Weather - </strong>What is the <a href="https://www.weather.gov/" id="https://www.weather.gov/|">weather forecast</a> for the duration of your trip? How will you prepare for it?</li>
<li><strong>Wildlife - </strong>What animals live in the park and how can you prepare for a chance encounter?</li>
<li><strong>Terrain - </strong>Are there uneven surfaces like unpaved trails or stairs you need to be aware of?</li>
<li><strong>Water - </strong>Are there currents or underwater hazards? Is the temperature of the water cold?</li>
<li><a href="https://www.nps.gov/planyourvisit/alerts.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/planyourvisit/alerts.htm|">Park Alerts</a> - Are there closures, hazards, or other active alerts that may affect your visit?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475341_3">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475341_3">
Find out what activities you can do at the park
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475341_3"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475341_3">
<p>There is more than one way to experience the park. Find a complete list of activities on the park's website under the "Things to do" page under the <a href="https://www.nps.gov/planyourvisit/index.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/planyourvisit/index.htm|">Plan Your Visit</a> page. Explore the pages of the activities that interest you. Find out if the park has Ranger-guided and <a href="https://www.nps.gov/kids/become-a-junior-ranger.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/kids/become-a-junior-ranger.htm|">Junior Ranger programs</a> and consider participating in them. </p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475344_4">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475344_4">
Know your limits
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475344_4"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475344_4">
<p>Your experience in the park is yours to decide. Only you know your abilities and your comfort level. Assess the following about yourself:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Skills - </strong>What outdoor skills do you have? Have you used them in a park like the one you're visiting?</li>
<li><strong>Experience - </strong> How often do you recreate outdoors? Have you recreated in a park like the one you're visiting?</li>
<li><strong>*Physical Fitness - </strong>Are you physically fit for your trip? Are there any activities that are beyond your abilities?</li>
<li><strong>*Medical Condition - </strong>Do you have a medical condition that could be worsened by the weather, altitude, or physical exertion?</li>
</ul>
*Consult a physician if you have any questions on fitness levels, health conditions, or medications required.
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475348_5">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475348_5">
Pick the right activity for YOU
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475348_5"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475348_5">
<p>There is more than one trail to hike, river to paddle, or mountain to climb.  Pick an activity that you can safely enjoy during your visit.  As you build your skills and experience, you can keep challenging yourself. Consider the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Weather - </strong>Will the weather make the activity more difficult? How can you prepare for it?</li>
<li><strong>Duration - </strong> How long will it take you to complete the activity? Do you have the physical fitness and endurance for it?</li>
<li><strong>Difficulty - </strong>What is the difficulty level of the activity you'd like to do? Is it within your limits and comfort level?</li>
<li><strong>Skill - </strong>Does the activity require special skills (e.g., rock climbing)? Do you have that skill? If not, how will you learn it before the trip?</li>
<li><strong>Gear - </strong>Does the activity require special gear (e.g., life jacket, helmet)? Do you have or can you obtain the right gear?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475369_6">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475369_6">
Look for regulations, permits, and reservations needed for your activity
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475369_6"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475369_6">
<ul>
<li><strong>Regulations - </strong>Regulations, restrictions, and closures protect park resources and keep visitors safe. Find out more about these rules under “Learn About the Park” on the park’s website.</li>
<li><strong>Permits - </strong>Find out if a permit is required for your activity under “Plan Your Visit”.  Follow the park’s instructions on how to apply and obtain a permit. </li>
<li><strong>Reservations - </strong>Some parks require reservations to enter the park, access an area of the park, and participate in an activity. All reservations can be made on <a href="https://www.recreation.gov/" id="https://www.recreation.gov/|">Recreation.gov</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475371_7">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475371_7">
Create a backup plan
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475371_7"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475371_7">
<p>Sometimes things don't go as planned. The weather forecast changes. Parking lots are full. Areas in the park close. You forget to pack an essential gear for the activity. Or you just simply don't feel up to the activity you planned. Choose a backup activity that will allow you to enjoy the park and not cancel the trip altogether. <br />
<br />
Note: Indoor activities are great backup plan options such as: park museums, historical buildings, and interpretive exhibits. They involve light physical activity and require no special gear. </p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475373_8">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475373_8">
Pack the 10 Essentials
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475373_8"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475373_8">
<p>The <a href="https://www.nps.gov/articles/10essentials.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/articles/10essentials.htm|">10 Essentials</a> are a collection of first aid and emergency items that can help you in the event of minor injuries, sudden weather changes, or unexpected delays.Your cell phone is not a substitute for any of the 10 essentials. You may not have service in the park and the battery may not last the whole trip.  <br />
<br />
Customize the 10 Essentials to your trip! You may need to pack additional items like medication, bug repellant, hiking boots, a life jacket, or a helmet. Consider packing a whistle for yourself and each person, especially if you are traveling with kids. If someone becomes lost, blowing a whistle can help search parties find them. Make sure that you can use your equipment properly and it works or fits correctly. <br />
<br />
Note: The <a href="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/digital/nps-apps.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/digital/nps-apps.htm|">NPS app</a> has park maps that can be downloaded for offline use. Always carry a backup paper map. Your phone battery may not last the whole trip and you could damage or lose your phone.  </p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475375_9">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475375_9">
Share your Trip Plan
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475375_9"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475375_9">
<p>Tell a Trusted Contact — who is not going on the trip with you — where you are going, what you are doing, and when you will be back. Ask them to call authorities and share your Trip Plan if you are not back from your trip on time. A Trip Plan has information that helps authorities respond if an emergency occurs or if you don’t return from your trip on time. <br />
<br />
Use the <a href="https://www.nps.gov/articles/gtgtripplan.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/articles/gtgtripplan.htm|">fillable Trip Plan</a> template or create your own. </p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475378_10">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475378_10">
Make an Outdoor Emergency Plan
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475378_10"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475378_10">
<p>Accidents happen. You may become lost or injured while recreating outdoors. Read the <a href="https://www.nps.gov/articles/gtgemergencyplan.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/articles/gtgemergencyplan.htm|">Outdoor Emergency Plan</a> to learn how to prevent becoming lost or injured and what to do in the event of an emergency. </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<style>
/* Keep your spacing for the component wrapper */
.Component.accordion-list-component { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
/* Progressive enhancement for browsers that support content-visibility */
@supports (content-visibility: hidden) {
/* Closed but searchable state */
.usa-accordion__content[hidden="until-found"] {
/* Must be "in layout" so Ctrl+F can match text */
display: block !important;
/* Don't paint and don't occupy space */
content-visibility: hidden;
height: 0 !important;
overflow: clip !important;
/* Kill the gap from defaults */
padding: 0 !important;
margin: 0 !important;
border: 0 !important;
/* Optional: avoid reserving intrinsic size */
contain-intrinsic-size: 0 0;
}
/* When opened, the [hidden] attribute is removed, so USWDS defaults return.
No extra "is-open" class is required. */
}
</style>
<script>
(function () {
// Enhance USWDS accordions with hidden="until-found" + beforematch support
function enhanceUSWDSUntilFound(root = document) {
// Panels we want to be searchable even when collapsed
const panels = root.querySelectorAll('.usa-accordion__content[hidden="until-found"]');
panels.forEach((panel) => {
const id = panel.id;
if (!id) return;
// Find the controlling button via aria-controls
const btn = root.querySelector('.usa-accordion__button[aria-controls="' + id + '"]');
if (!btn) return;
// Keep the DOM state in sync with the button's aria-expanded
const sync = () => {
const expanded = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
if (expanded) {
panel.removeAttribute('hidden');     // let USWDS show it
panel.classList.add('is-open');
} else {
// Re-apply our special attribute so Ctrl+F can still find text
panel.setAttribute('hidden', 'until-found');
panel.classList.remove('is-open');
}
};
// 1) When a Find-in-Page match hits hidden content, open its panel
if ('onbeforematch' in document.body) {
panel.addEventListener('beforematch', () => {
// USWDS toggles on click; only click if currently collapsed
if (btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'false') {
btn.click();
}
});
}
// 2) Observe USWDS state changes (it toggles aria-expanded on the button)
const mo = new MutationObserver(sync);
mo.observe(btn, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['aria-expanded'] });
// 3) Initial sync (after USWDS init)
queueMicrotask(sync);
// 4) Also resync on click in case MutationObserver misses anything
btn.addEventListener('click', () => setTimeout(sync, 0));
});
}
if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => enhanceUSWDSUntilFound());
} else {
enhanceUSWDSUntilFound();
}
})();
</script></div><a id="AATP"></a><a id="CP_JUMP_7481437"></a><div id="cs_control_7481437" class="cs_control CS_Element_Custom"><style>blockquote {border-left: 5px solid #fff;}</style>
<div class="Component ArticleTextGroup TextWrapped clearfix">
<p> </p>
<h2>Arrival at the Park</h2>
</div></div><div id="cs_control_5853034" class="cs_control CS_Element_Custom"><style>blockquote {border-left: 5px solid #fff;}</style>
<div class="Component ArticleTextGroup TextWrapped clearfix">
<figure class="-auto-width">
<picture>
<source type="image/webp" srcset="/subjects/healthandsafety/images/AATP_banner_text.png?maxwidth=1300&autorotate=false&quality=78&format=webp">
<img alt="A graphic of two visitors talking to a park ranger at a visitor center. On the left, a sign reads &quot;Step Two.&quot;" src="/subjects/healthandsafety/images/AATP_banner_text.png?maxwidth=1300&autorotate=false" title="Arrival at the Park Banner"  >
</picture>
</figure><!-- floating-image alignment  -->
<h4>So you’ve made it to the park, what next?</h4>
<p>Keep reading to find out what you should do when you get to the park, and what to "Ask a Ranger" before you start your activity:</p>
</div></div><div id="cs_control_7475392" class="cs_control CS_Element_BulletedList"><div class="Component accordion-list-component">
<div id="accordion7475392" class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered">
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475424_2">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475424_2">
Check park conditions
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475424_2"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475424_2">
<p>Stop by a Visitor Center or Ranger Station if available. Ask a Ranger about the latest park conditions including weather forecast, active alerts, and closures. You can also visit the park’s website, download the NPS mobile app, or follow the park on social media for current information.<br />
<br />
Questions you can "Ask a Ranger":</p>
<ul>
<li>Are any areas closed? Roads, trails, campsites, etc. </li>
<li>What's the weather forecast? Lightning, high temperatures, snow, etc. </li>
<li>Is there animal activity? Sightings, increased activity, etc. </li>
<li>Are there other alers? Fires, water levels, air quality, etc. </li>
<li>Where can I find drinking water? Visitor center, along trails, etc. </li>
</ul>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475425_3">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475425_3">
Check the 10 Essentials and your gear
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475425_3"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475425_3">
Confirm that you have packed the <a href="javascript:HandleLink('cpe_7475392_3','CPNEWWIN:_blank^@https://www.nps.gov/articles/10essentials.htm');" id="CPNEWWIN:_blank^@https://www.nps.gov/articles/10essentials.htm|" onmouseout=" return window.status=''; " onmouseover=" return window.status='https://www.nps.gov/articles/10essentials.htm'; ">10 Essentials</a> and any additional gear necessary for your activity.
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475426_4">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475426_4">
Ask yourself: are you ready for your activity?
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475426_4"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475426_4">
How are you feeling? Do you have the energy needed for your activity? Remember that you have a backup activity you can do. 
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475427_5">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475427_5">
Put your backup plan into action, if necessary
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475427_5"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475427_5">
<p>Implement your backup plan if:</p>
<ul>
<li>Park conditions have changed </li>
<li>You don't have the right gear and supplies</li>
<li>You're not feeling up to the planned activity</li>
</ul>
<strong>Notify your Trip Plan Trusted Contact of your change of plans. </strong>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475431_6">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475431_6">
Pick up permits
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475431_6"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475431_6">
<p>If a permit is required for your activity, get the permit, pay permit fees, and read all regulations and safety information. </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<style>
/* Keep your spacing for the component wrapper */
.Component.accordion-list-component { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
