<div class="Component ArticleTextGroup TextWrapped clearfix">
<p> </p>
<h2>During the Trip</h2>
</div></div><div id="cs_control_7475433" class="cs_control CS_Element_Custom"><style>blockquote {border-left: 5px solid #fff;}</style>
<div class="Component ArticleTextGroup TextWrapped clearfix">
<figure class="-auto-width">
<picture>
<source type="image/webp" srcset="/subjects/healthandsafety/images/DTT_banner_text.png?maxwidth=1300&autorotate=false&quality=78&format=webp">
<img alt="A visitor wearing a helmet is riding a bike on a trail. To their left, a visitor is sitting on a bench. On the left, a sign reads &quot;Step Three.&quot;" src="/subjects/healthandsafety/images/DTT_banner_text.png?maxwidth=1300&autorotate=false" title="During the Trip"  >
</picture>
</figure><!-- floating-image alignment  -->
<h4>You’re doing great!</h4>
<p>Whether it's on your hike or paddling down a river, keep these tips in mind while recreating in the park:</p>
</div></div><div id="cs_control_7475435" class="cs_control CS_Element_BulletedList"><div class="Component accordion-list-component">
<div id="accordion7475435" class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered">
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475437_2">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475437_2">
Stick to your plan
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475437_2"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475437_2">
<p>If you change your itinerary or route from the one noted on your Trip Plan, your Trusted Contact will not know where you are. Search and Rescue authorities may have trouble finding you.<br />
<br />
<strong>If a safety concern impacts your activity, consider turning around instead of pushing ahead. </strong></p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475439_3">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475439_3">
Stay within designated areas
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475439_3"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475439_3">
<p>Stay on the trail, within established campsites, and other designated areas.  You will reduce the risk of becoming lost and injured while protecting the natural resources around you.</p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475440_4">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475440_4">
Stay together
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475440_4"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475440_4">
<p><strong>If you are traveling with a group, stay together. If you must leave the group, use the buddy system. </strong>Separation could lead to getting lost or injured. Refer to the <a href="https://www.nps.gov/articles/gtgemergencyplan.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/articles/gtgemergencyplan.htm|">Outdoor Emergency Plan</a> for more tips on how to avoid becoming lost or injured. </p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475441_5">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475441_5">
Stay aware of your surroundings
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475441_5"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475441_5">
<ul>
<li>Watch your step</li>
<li>Stay alert for wildlife activity</li>
<li>Keep an eye on the weather</li>
<li><a href="https://www.nps.gov/orgs/1563/submit-a-tip.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/orgs/1563/submit-a-tip.htm|">Report</a> suspicious activity</li>
</ul>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475442_6">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475442_6">
Keep a safe distance from wildlife
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475442_6"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475442_6">
<p>Parks are not petting zoos. Many parks require you to stay a minimum distance of 25 to 50 yards from most wildlife and 100 yards from predators like bears and wolves. If you’re close enough for a selfie, you’re definitely too close. Use binoculars or your camera lens to observe wildlife. When you follow <a href="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/watchingwildlife/index.htm" id="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/watchingwildlife/index.htm|">safe wildlife watching practices</a>, you protect the health of the wildlife and yourself. </p>
</div>
<h4 class="usa-accordion__heading" id="heading_7475443_7">
<button class="usa-accordion__button"
type="button"
aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="body_7475443_7">
Check in with yourself: should you continue your activity?
</button>
</h4>
<div id="body_7475443_7"
class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose"
hidden="until-found"
aria-labelledby="heading_7475443_7">
<p>Assess how you feel and if you should continue with your planned activity. Is it time to take a break? Should you turn around? <u>If something doesn't feel right, don't do it.</u><strong> </strong>You can always visit the park on a day when you are feeling better. </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<style>
/* Keep your spacing for the component wrapper */
.Component.accordion-list-component { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
/* Progressive enhancement for browsers that support content-visibility */
